From: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: preserve TTL for bridge offload

XG2010G LAN1/LAN2 same-subnet tests show TCP packets arriving with TTL
127 from a Windows host whose initial TTL is 128. Stopping bridger removes
the TC/PPE rules and restores TTL 128 on the identical path.

Do not enable TTL decrement for the L2 template. IPv4 and IPv6 subflows
inherit the template control bits, while routed entries retain their
existing decrement behavior. This does not change NBQ or flow lifetime.

Signed-off-by: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -357,8 +357,10 @@
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_UDP, l4proto == IPPROTO_UDP) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_VLAN_LAYER, data->vlan.num) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_VPM, data->vlan.num) |
-	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PPPOE, data->pppoe.num) |
-	      AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL;
+	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PPPOE, data->pppoe.num);
+	/* L2 subflows inherit this template, including TTL handling. */
+	if (type != PPE_PKT_TYPE_BRIDGE)
+		val |= AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL;
 	hwe->ib1 = val;
 
 	val = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PORT_AG, 0x1f);
